M5 (wip): verification depth -- coverage, latency, stress, metrics

Stimulus and checking:
  - tb/common/coverage.py: hand-rolled functional coverage with the bins
    derived from the schema, and a reachability rule so the denominator
    contains only bins that can be hit.
  - 1.1 MB of randomised traffic through the DUT per configuration, batched
    with a fresh traffic shape each time.
  - malformed corpus grown from 13 cases to 31, plus misplaced tlast.
  - tests/test_vectors.py: 99 checks over hand-authored byte vectors with
    hand-computed expected values, and byte maps that pin which byte feeds
    which field.
  - latency is now asserted per record against the beat that releases it,
    rather than the beat that completes it -- see the comment in
    test_parser_feed.py for why that is the right reference.

Defects found and fixed:
  - B009 a trailing fragment on the packet's last beat was never classified,
        so the verdict depended on DATA_W rather than on the packet.
  - B010 a runt packet's verdict landed a cycle early and overwrote its
        predecessor's; a packet could be parsed and never reported.
  - B011 skip mode entered on the last beat never expired, so a message
        declaring 65,537 bytes finished clean.

Metrics:
  - ci/check.sh writes metrics.json every run, merged from per-stage
    fragments in build/metrics/.
  - ci/collect_metrics.py: static size and defect facts plus measured ones.
  - ci/mutate.py: mutation testing harness (not yet run).
